                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A charming no-frills more laid back metroidvania. One of the gimmicks is that you have to learn a little mini-language made up of musical notes, entering the notes can be tedious, but trying to figure out how the language works is engaging if unnecessary. It adds a little something to exploration when you find a rune that lets you say many more words than you could before. The core gameplay and monster design is pretty simple, but If you like to collect everything there is enough to collect to pad out your playtime quite a bit. The level design is pretty strong, with each room having its own character. Some of the secrets are pretty hard to find without a guide.",
